# `a` enters the outermost head as the written 0, so its row begins with a guess, int[0, 2^53], and the guess enters the heads inside. What comes round there is a meeting block's parameter: the head's own parameter, guess and all, beside an int32.
# What is noted, handed up the heads and climbed from is what comes round BESIDE the parameter: meeting blocks, handlers' blocks and the entries of finished loops are looked through, also for what ENTERS a head inside; a value
# that holds more than the parameter and what stood beside counts whole. A row inside that fitted under the guess starts its next walk from what enters then. The sums ended as int[-2^53, 2^53] @Int64 at every head.
# f3 = inside, f4 = inFront, f5 = threeDeep, f6 = behindHandler
# OPTIONS: check=Validate
# RUN: walk f3 f4 f5 f6 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f3:Body
# CHECK-NOT: int[-9007199254740992
# CHECK-LABEL: code f4:Body
# CHECK-NOT: int[-9007199254740992
# CHECK-LABEL: code f5:Body
# CHECK-NOT: int[-9007199254740992
# CHECK-LABEL: code f6:Body
# CHECK-NOT: int[-9007199254740992
